# Build context filter for stacks/wall/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` before the context root's `.dockerignore`,
# which is what lets this stack carry its own filter without putting a file at the repo root
# that every other build would then inherit.
#
# The context is the WHOLE REPO, because the image needs src/, web/, db/ and the entry point.
# Unfiltered that is ~93 MB, most of it Home Assistant's icon cache and a node_modules tree
# that `npm ci` is about to rebuild anyway — sent over the daemon socket on every build, and
# invalidating the cache whenever any of it changes.

# The sibling stack's runtime state. Thousands of cached brand icons, a SQLite database, and
# the household's actual Home Assistant configuration — none of which belongs in an image.
stacks/homeassistant/

# Rebuilt inside the image against this exact base. Copying the host's would ship a
# better-sqlite3 compiled for the host's libc.
node_modules/

# Built inside the image by `npm run build`.
web/dist/

.git/
.gitignore

# Local databases and their WAL sidecars. The real one is a volume.
dev.db*
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Secrets never enter a build context, resolved or otherwise.
.env
op.env
**/op.env

# Nothing here changes what the server does.
docs/
pi/
test/
README.md
CLAUDE.md
